- **The fence (plumbing).** Copy `fence-preload.js` from `session-tools/b807/` to `session-tools/b837/instrument/`, `cmp`, and prove its sha256. **Write your own `fence-quiet.js`** (same redirection of any fs call under `/tmp/printer-dashboard-data` into a shadow tree, records to a log FILE, prints nothing on stdout: the stock fence's exit line breaks neighbour files that parse a child's stdout); control: a planted mkdir plus write plus exists on the shared path is redirected and logged, the real directory keeps its stat, an ordinary write passes. Every jest run of yours uses it through `NODE_OPTIONS='-r <fence-quiet.js>'`. The cells start the real server as a CHILD: confirm the child inherits the fence (`NODE_OPTIONS` is inherited by `spawn` with no `env` override; read the test's `spawn` call for its `env`, and say whether the fence reaches the child; if it does not, the shared directory read before and after is the evidence, C6).
- **Your own instruments, written by you, read back, scanned for non-ASCII:** (i) the **cell runner** (jest, `--runInBand` for single files, `--json --outputFile`, fenced); (ii) the **cell table extractor** (a `python3 -I` reader of the jest JSON that prints, per cell, title, status and the first failure line; two tables are compared as multisets of (title, status)); (iii) the **diff and hygiene checker** (C1); (iv) the **mutant generator** (plain text swaps of a scratch copy in ONE tree `worktrees/b837-mut`, anchor count 1 each, restore by writing `git show origin/b835:<path>` over the file and proving blob equality and `git diff --quiet`, never `checkout --`; a variant whose anchor is missing reports NOT-LANDED, never a kill; a variant that does not load or whose server does not boot reports that, never a kill: a mutant that breaks the boot reddens every cell, say "boot failure", not "killed"); (v) the **word counter** (C3: counts of the 400 sentence and the 200 message in `server.js` at main, head and under each mutant, with a control that changes the count).

