## GRADING (binding; the ONE table; capability decides)
- **G-1 delta (C1, C3).** A path beyond the three, a backend byte beyond the three added lines, a validator, reader or scheduler file in the diff, a workflow, `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, `verify-suite.sh`, a changed word (the 400 sentence or the 200 message), a touched red-flag line, or the counts file moving more than `tests`/`suites`/`_updated` = **Blocker**; a removed line beyond the three counts lines, or a lost/added/renamed cell beyond the 21, `.only/.skip/.todo`, a retry, a suppression comment = **Major**; a person's name, real customer name, secret or decision-card id in an added line or the message = **Blocker**; a brief or work number token in an added line = **Minor**; non-ASCII in the added lines = **Major**; a head other than `a055bd63` = STOP; one commit = **Note** (a merge commit of the gated head keeps it: C-190, C-68).
- **G-2 the cells prove the change (C4, C5).** An E1/E2/E5 cell green at main = **Major**; any cell red at the head on the unbroken product = **Major**; a named mutant (G-M1..G-M10) not turning its named cells red = **Major**; a cell family with no reddening mutant and not a named control = **Major**; the table differing between two head runs = **Major**; G-M11 surviving = **Note** (the builder declared falsy levels out of scope; RD-892's subject), unless a cell in a neighbour file turns red under it (then report which); G-M12 equivalent = no finding.
- **G-3 behaviour (C3, C7).** A way to store a mixed-case level after the change = **Major**; a way to store a level the check refuses = **Blocker and a hand-up**; the typeof guard missing a case the check lets through (a falsy non-string reaching `.toLowerCase()`) = **Major**; the statement before the check or after the store call = **Major**; a reader or the scheduler changed = **Blocker**.
- **G-4 CodeQL and CI (C9, C11).** **An open alert on the PR ref at a line the PR added = Blocker for the landing** (the `CodeQL` check fails and the ruleset's thresholds block the merge; record each alert, its rule and severity); an open alert on a line the PR did not add = reported, not this PR's; a failing check-run on the head other than `CodeQL` = **Major**; `in_progress` at the verdict = `CI pending: <names>`, conditional; the verify pair differing from the committed counts file in either direction = **Blocker**; a whole-suite red you reproduce twice = **Major**; a textual conflict = **Major**; a path shared with another open PR or live lane = **Major**. **Always Note:** the author field, a dependabot vulnerabilities line, the stored mixed-case rows that stay skipped until their next save (L5), the empty-string and falsy levels (RD-892), the uncleaned `nexusai-rd893-*` temp directories, the Linux runner and node 24 if the hosted `build` is not complete, the builder's local node v26.
- **G-5 the verdict follows the table, and the cap.** Any Blocker or Major = `NO GO round 1 of 2`: FOR TUESDAY then carries the CLOSED list (the sites and cells you proved, with the cells that prove them), the RESIDUE as ticket text, and the fix shape in prose (one new commit on the same branch, forward only, no rebase; a new head is a new gate round 2 of 2 and a new CodeQL run). Notes and Minors only = `GO` or `GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS`. Add ` (conditional: <reason>)` for any required check not run; `CI pending` is always conditional. `model-routing.md:111` (G-cap): "Two NO GO rounds on one class: STOP. Ship the closed instances, ticket the residue with the tester's cells attached. A third round needs [the product owner]'s word on a card." The landing is a merge commit, so the commit message, not the PR title, becomes history: say which text lands.

